  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, 15 January 1930; only one candidate was nominated and the five other retiring members were deemed elected, so there was no contest (Larne Times, 11 January 1930, p. 3). John Hunter was the only candidate nominated. The paper adds that the other retiring members, 'although not nominated, will be deemed to be duly elected'. Returned unopposed."
